// ── Density: the constraint that actually governs this surface ──────────────────────────────────
// A 1280×720 share is small, and it is read in someone else's video tile while a person talks over
// it. Measured: ~11 blocks forces a 0.65 scale, at which 15px body text renders ~10px — present, but
// not readable at a glance, which is the only kind of reading that happens here.
//
// So the schema is deliberately richer than any single screen should use. Six to eight blocks is the
// working ceiling; past that the producer should DROP the least-live block rather than let the
// renderer shrink everything. Showing less is the feature.
